    "updated_at": "2019-05-14T04:42:46Z",
    "body": "You definitely bring up some good points. 🤔\r\n\r\nThe \"✨🚀\" pairing was meant to literally be \"star ship\", but I'm open to picking emojis that differently interpret the meaning of the project.\r\n\r\nOne problem we encounter is that the representation of the `:comet:` emoji differs greatly between implementations. On macOS, the emojis would look like this:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4658208/57671068-62eead80-75cf-11e9-8589-9474d0f32180.png)\r\n\r\nThis representation doesn't quite look as much like a \"warp-bubble as a blurry streak across space\". That being said, it does look nice with the emoji set that GitHub falls back on (as is shown in your screenshots).",
